CALCULATIONS AND BUSINESS LOGIC (pure, tested functions in /src/lib/calculations.ts)
- All period boundaries and the "today" calculation use Asia/Jakarta. Weeks run Monday-Sunday. "Bulan ini" runs from the 1st to the last day of the month. Custom ranges are inclusive by dateKey.
- Total income = sum of income transactions in range. Total expense = sum of expense transactions in range. Net balance = income − expense. Available balance on the dashboard = all-time income − all-time expense for the selected workspace (not limited to the period).
- Budget used = sum of EXPENSE transactions with dateKey between budget start and end (inclusive) and, for category limits, matching the category; in group scope only the group's transactions. Income is never counted as spending and never reduces a budget; no double-counting. Remaining = amount − used (may be negative). Percentage = used / amount × 100.
- Average daily spending = used / elapsed days (min 1). Projected remaining money at period end = remaining − (avg daily × remaining days); "safe daily spend" = remaining / remaining days.
- Editing or deleting a transaction recomputes everything immediately via snapshot listeners.
- Alerts: thresholds 70% (Peringatan awal, info), 85% (Peringatan penting, warning), 100% (Anggaran habis, danger), >100% (Anggaran terlampaui, danger). Evaluate after every transaction change; write a notification only if the deterministic ID doesn't exist yet (create-only, no repeats). Show the highest active alert on the dashboard and all in the notifications page with unread badge. Handle the case where deleting a transaction drops usage below a threshold (alerts remain in history but the dashboard shows only the current state).
- Evaluasi Keuangan (computed only from real stored transactions; show an empty state when there is no data): remaining budget, top spending category with its share, comparison with the previous equivalent period (absolute and %), average daily spending, safe daily limit, and rule-based recommendations, e.g.: if projected overspend, suggest the exact daily cap; if a category exceeds its limit or its usual share, suggest reducing it with a computed amount; if there is leftover budget, suggest saving a computed amount to Tabungan. Every recommendation must cite the real numbers behind it.
- Validation: amount > 0 (integer), required category and date, note max 200 chars, budget start ≤ end, budget amount > 0, no overlapping duplicate-active budget of the same scope and period type unless intended, confirm dialog before any delete. Use react-hook-form + zod with Indonesian error messages.
- No dummy data may ever mix with real user data. Optionally offer a clearly labeled "Mode Demo" that runs on an in-memory, read-only sample dataset and never touches Firestore.

